        "eyebrow": "My story",
        "heading": "Behind the lens",
        "signature": "Joseph Rowland",
        "signature_asset": "about-joseph-signature.png",
        "text": "<p>I’m Joseph Rowland, a photographer based on Long Island, New York. My love of photography began in high school with a Pentax K1000 and the anticipation of watching an image emerge in the darkroom. That fascination has stayed with me ever since, taking me from familiar shores close to home to mountain ranges, forest trails, and city streets across the country.</p><p>What draws me to a scene is often the light: the last glow of sunset reflected across West Meadow Beach, sunlight slipping through the windows of Grand Central, or clouds briefly lifting to reveal a mountain peak. Sometimes a photograph takes planning, patience, and a long drive. Other times, it begins with simply stopping to notice something beautiful.</p><p>My work spans landscapes, wildlife, architecture, and everyday moments, but the thread running through it is a desire to capture how a place feels—the stillness, the scale, the wonder—and leave room for you to find your own connection.</p><p>For me, one of the greatest joys of photography is turning an image into a print. There’s something deeply satisfying about holding a photograph in your hands and seeing its details, colors, and textures come to life on paper. I especially love a beautifully matted and framed print. The mat gives the image space to breathe, and the frame brings it all together. Hanging it on a wall completes a journey that began with a moment behind the camera.</p><p>Having operated a photography gallery in Port Jefferson, I’ve also experienced the pleasure of helping someone find a photograph they want to live with. That’s the spirit behind Rowland Photography: sharing images that have stayed with me, thoughtfully presented so they can become part of your home.</p><p>I hope you find something here that makes you pause, brings back a memory, or invites you somewhere new.</p>",
